Subject: [PATCH] agent: preserve radio state when replying to client capability queries

A client capability query is a synchronous read/reply, not completion of
radio onboarding. The handler nevertheless marked its radio configured,
including when report validation or transmission failed. During the 0905
appliance reboot, early backhaul-client queries hit two extender radios
before their WSC exchange. Those radios skipped configuration and the
controller remained at 34 rather than 50 BSS records.

Reply without changing the radio state. This also preserves pending M2,
OneWifi configuration, topology synchronization and steering transactions
when an unrelated capability query arrives. Retain the existing reply,
message identifier, validation and failure reporting paths.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 src/em/capability/em_capability.cpp | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/em/capability/em_capability.cpp b/src/em/capability/em_capability.cpp
--- a/src/em/capability/em_capability.cpp
+++ b/src/em/capability/em_capability.cpp
@@ -965,7 +965,6 @@ void em_capability_t::handle_client_cap_query(unsigned char *buff, unsigned int len)
         em_printfout("Client cap report send failed for sta=%s",
                 util::mac_to_string(sta).c_str());
     }
-    set_state(em_state_agent_configured);
 }
 
 int em_capability_t::handle_bsta_cap_query(unsigned char *buff, unsigned int len)
